= Ring Theory

== Introduction
Ring theory studies algebraic structures with two binary operations: addition and multiplication. Rings generalize the arithmetic of integers. They are crucial in cryptography because most cryptographic algorithms (like RSA, AES, ECC) operate over specific finite rings or fields (which are special types of rings).

